## Source audit follow-up

The added Java fixture cases pin the neighboring `ProcessQueue.cleanExpiredMsg`
branches: missing and empty `CONSUME_START_TIME` skip expiry; Java Unicode
decimal digits are accepted by `Long.parseLong`; orderly mode returns before
parsing malformed values. Rust tests compare those outcomes with the invoked
Java fixture. The fixture SHA-256 is
`0ecf6ca6795174a96a90123cebb5415c2108cc81842ce84469e721d599f90d01`.

This follow-up changes only the Java fixture, Rust assertions and compatibility
documents; the runtime implementation remains `9147a902`. The earlier pinned
source/error and retry work is recorded in
`rlogs/2026/09/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate__20261021T162010Z.rlog`.

